course: dictionary
lesson: 848
title: One word, many meanings: bet
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. «Bet» is a good example. As a verb, to bet means to risk money or something on what will happen. As a noun, a bet is that agreement, or the money risked.
explain: «I bet it rains.» Here bet does not mean risking money. It means I am sure, or I think it is very likely. Ask yourself: is anyone putting money on the line? If not, it is the "I am sure" meaning.
explain: «A good bet» means a good choice, and «your best bet» means the wisest option. In maths, bets link to chance: likely, unlikely or certain. Always check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence.
explain: Be careful, because real bets need agreement. «A bet needs both people to agree; nobody owes anything for a deal they never accepted.» A dare such as «If you don't climb on the roof, you owe me a fiver» is not a real bet, and risky stunts are dangerous.
fact: «Bet» can be a verb (to bet) or a noun (a bet).
fact: «I bet» means «I am sure» or «I think it is very likely».
fact: «Gambling» means betting money on something you cannot control, and it is only legal for adults.
fact: «Gambling addiction» means a person keeps betting to win back losses, which can lead to debt and family arguments; help exists from doctors and charities.
fact: «You bet!» means «certainly!», especially in North America.
exercise: «I bet it rains before lunch.» What does bet mean here? | * I am sure it will rain | I hope the sun comes out | I am risking money on the weather | I am betting my lunch
exercise: «Your best bet is to take the umbrella.» What does best bet mean? | * A good choice | A competition with prizes | A loud shout | A risky stunt
exercise: Which one is a real bet? | You owe me a fiver because I said so, and I never agreed to it | * Two people agree to bet a pound on the score, and the winner gets the money | Your friend says a dare is a deal | Nobody agrees, but you owe money anyway
test: «Gambling means betting money on something you cannot control.» What does gambling mean? | Playing a game with friends for fun | Sharing your lunch | Saving money in a bank | * Betting money on something you cannot control
test: Is «I bet» in «I bet she is late» about money? | No, it means I am angry | Yes, only when the bet is a dare | Yes, it always means money is risked | * No, it means I am sure or very likely
exam: Which sentence uses bet to mean a risk of money that two people agreed to? | * «A bet needs both people to agree; nobody owes anything for a deal they never accepted.» | «I bet you that our team wins the match, and the loser pays a pound.» | «I bet she is cold in that jumper.» | «You bet, that is certainly right!»
